#4471 merged **412 reports** as "dates parse mm/dd in eu locales". The export has 427 rows,
but 15 are duplicates of the same report id, so 412 is the real count. The reports do not
share one cause. They split into three problems, and only the first one is fixed.

<Callout kind="warn">
The desk update says "parser fixed, hint won't fix because booking-v3 is retired". Both
halves need a second look: the parser fix covers one problem of two, and three tenants
still run booking-v3.
</Callout>

## Causes, computed from the data

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The cause comes from the **tenant**: its locale and the booking form it runs. It does not
come from intake's tag, which is a guess from the reporter's browser. Intake tagged 23
parser reports as `hint` and 15 hint reports as `parser`.

## The three problems

| problem | reports | ticket |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Shared parser reads every date month-first | 374 | [#71](https://github.com/piotrczarnak/mega/issues/71) |
| booking-v3 form hints MM/DD/YYYY to day-first tenants | 33 | [#72](https://github.com/piotrczarnak/mega/issues/72) |
| Bookings move by one day, not a month flip | 5 | [#73](https://github.com/piotrczarnak/mega/issues/73) |

374 + 33 + 5 = 412.

### 1. Parser, 374 reports

The shared parser reads every date month first, so day-first tenants get flipped dates. It
hit all 11 day-first tenants, through the app, email and the form. The desk fix
`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` addresses this problem.


### 2. Form hint, 33 reports

booking-v3 prints a `MM/DD/YYYY` hint. People type what the hint says and the form reads it
day first. Only tenants on booking-v3 with a day-first locale are affected: alder.physio
(12), copper.studio (11) and pale.harbour (10). All 33 came in through the form.

**Not fixed, and not retired.** The desk closed this as "won't fix: form retired", yet these
three tenants still run booking-v3. The parser fix does not change what the hint prints.

### 3. One-day move, 5 reports

R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 describe a booking that is exactly one day
off, or an invite that arrived before the booking. That is not a month/day swap, so the
parser fix does not explain it. The pattern suggests a time zone or daylight-saving shift.
Intake tagged all five as `parser`. The cause is not confirmed; engineering needs to
reproduce it.

## Lessons

- A big ticket is not always one bug reported many times. Split by cause before you call it known.
- Count unique report ids. The export overlaps pages and counted 15 reports twice.
- Find the cause from the tenant's locale and form, not from intake's tag.
- "Won't fix" needs a check: is the thing really gone?

